    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "139f3294_80cd9a9e",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/server/ConnectivityService.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 5995,
      "author": {
        "id": 1306837
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-12-21T06:55:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It seems to me this method checks whether the uid has permission to access restricted network,\nwhile getAllowedUids checks if the uid can access the restricted network without the permission. I think that is somehow different, but it seems to me use getAllowedUids here is more correct.\n\nBut we\u0027ll need Jean\u0027s comment. Jean would have more context about this.",
      "parentUuid": "48aea3b8_bb91b1c5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 5995,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 5995,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "021d34acd30555fe3f3231ea23746dc34aa20be7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7e4421b1_d6d1a266",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/server/ConnectivityService.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 5995,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-05T08:27:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this is the correct method to call. Junyu\u0027s comments are also correct in that :\n• this method checks whether the UID holds USE_RESTRICTED_NETWORKS.\n• getAllowedUids checks if the UID can access a network even without the permission.\n\nIn this case, we want to know if this network is restricted to this app. So :\n• If the network has NET_CAP_NOT_RESTRICTED ⇒ no\n• If the UID holds USE_RESTRICTED_NETWORKS ⇒ no\n• If the UID is in allowed UIDs ⇒ no\n• If the network is the default for this UID ⇒ no\n• Otherwise ⇒ yes\n\nSo it seems to me the logic in this patchset is missing the check for this network being the default for this UID, but is otherwise correct. Though I would suggest checking for `nc.isRestricted()` first because it\u0027s much faster and the most common case.\n\nAnother thing this might need to handle is the background permission ? Eventually the blocked status callback does need to reflect this too, but I don\u0027t remember if NPMS already handles this in the blocked reasons it sends ConnectivityService. See `#queryNetworkAccess` (though... I think we probably want to remove that one, really)",
      "parentUuid": "139f3294_80cd9a9e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 5995,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 5995,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "021d34acd30555fe3f3231ea23746dc34aa20be7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
